This file marks the one directory that keinepanikmusik.de is served from.

.github/workflows/deploy.yml checks over SSH that this file is in the target before
it runs rsync, because the hosting account carries several domains and each has its
own directory. A typo in HETZNER_PATH would not fail loudly — it would empty another
site. With the check, the deploy can only ever write into a directory that somebody
identified by hand.

Placed once, over SSH, in the directory konsoleH names as the document root for
keinepanikmusik.de:

    touch /path/to/that/directory/.keinepanik-webroot

After that it ships with every deploy, so --delete cannot remove it. Deleting it on
the server stops deploys until someone puts it back on purpose, which is the point:
the marker is the confirmation, not a formality.

It is never served — .htaccess denies every dotfile.
